      "questionNumber": 1,
      "stem": "Which of the following statements regarding target autoantigens and circulating biomarkers in primary membranous nephropathy is CORRECT?",
      "options": [
        "A. Anti-PLA2R autoantibodies target a podocyte surface membrane receptor and account for approximately 70–80% of primary membranous nephropathy cases.",
        "B. Anti-THSD7A autoantibodies represent the most frequent cause of secondary membranous nephropathy associated with systemic lupus erythematosus.",
        "C. Serum anti-PLA2R autoantibody titers typically lag behind clinical proteinuria reduction during treatment-induced disease remission.",
        "D. Complete absence of serum anti-PLA2R autoantibodies definitively excludes the diagnosis of primary membranous nephropathy."
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "A",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "【選項分析】\nA. 【正確】Primary Membranous Nephropathy 最主要的標的 Autoantigen 為位於 Podocyte 表面膜上的 PLA2R (Phospholipase A2 Receptor)，約佔 Primary Membranous Nephropathy 病例的 70–80%。檢測 Serum Anti-PLA2R Autoantibody 對於診斷、評估 Disease Activity 以及監測 Therapeutic Response 具有高度特異性與敏感性。\nB. 【錯誤】THSD7A (Thrombospondin Type-1 Domain-Containing 7A) 僅佔 Primary Membranous Nephropathy 的 1–5%，且常與 Underlying Malignancy 相關，而非 Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE) 引起的 Secondary Membranous Nephropathy。\nC. 【錯誤】Serum Anti-PLA2R Autoantibody 濃度的下降或轉陰 (Immunologic Remission) 通常會領先 (precede) Clinical Remission (Proteinuria 的改善與減少) 數月之久，而非滯後 (lag behind)。\nD. 【錯誤】約有 20–30% 的 Primary Membranous Nephropathy 病患為 Serum Anti-PLA2R Negative（可能由 THSD7A, NELL1, EXT1/EXT2, PCDH7, NCAM1 等其他 Autoantigen 所引致），因此 Serum Anti-PLA2R 陰性並不能完全排除 Primary Membranous Nephropathy 的診斷。",
      "resolvedImages": [
