      "questionNumber": 4,
      "stem": "An electron microscopy (EM) evaluation of a renal biopsy demonstrates electron-dense deposits located in the subepithelial space between the outer aspect of the glomerular basement membrane (GBM) and overlying podocyte foot processes, accompanied by basement membrane projections protruding between the deposits. Which stage of membranous nephropathy does this ultrastructural finding represent, and what is its classic appearance on Jones' methenamine silver stain?",
      "options": [
        "A. Stage I membranous nephropathy; presents with normal capillary loops without any GBM projections or silver-staining abnormalities.",
        "B. Stage III membranous nephropathy; presents with completely intramembranous lucent zones and loss of silver staining.",
        "C. Stage IV membranous nephropathy; presents with extensive GBM duplication and double-contour formation.",
        "D. Stage II membranous nephropathy; presents with a classic \"spike and hole\" pattern on silver stain."
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "D",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "【選項分析】\nA. 【錯誤】Stage I Membranous Nephropathy 在 EM 下僅有小範圍的 Subepithelial Electron-Dense Deposits，GBM 尚未出現明顯的 Base Membrane Projections (Spikes)，LM 銀染常接近正常。\nB. 【錯誤】Stage III Membranous Nephropathy 的 EM 特徵為 Subepithelial Deposits 已被新生的 GBM 材質完全包覆 (Intramembranous Deposits)。\nC. 【錯誤】Stage IV Membranous Nephropathy 為 Deposits 被吸收後留下的 Thickened, Irregular, Lucent GBM，銀染呈蟲蝕狀 (Moth-eaten Appearance)，而非 Double-contour (Double-contour 為 MPGN 特徵)。\nD. 【正確】Stage II Membranous Nephropathy 的 EM 特徵為大量的 Subepithelial Electron-Dense Deposits 位於 Podocyte 與 GBM 外側之間，且鄰近的 GBM 材質向上突起形成 Projections (Spikes)。在 Jones' Methenamine Silver Stain 下，這些向外延伸的黑尖刺與中間不著色的沉積物形成了經典的 \"Spike and Hole\" Pattern。",
      "resolvedImages": [
