      "questionNumber": 9,
      "stem": "A 61-year-old man with hypercalcemia (serum calcium 12.2 mg/dL), hypophosphatemia (serum phosphorus 2.1 mg/dL), and markedly elevated intact PTH (210 pg/mL) undergoes localization studies for primary hyperparathyroidism. Neck ultrasonography fails to identify any enlarged parathyroid gland. Technetium-99m (99mTc) Sestamibi SPECT/CT demonstrates a focal area of increased radiotracer uptake in the anterior mediastinum, which overlaps anatomically with multiple calcified mediastinal lymph nodes secondary to previous pulmonary tuberculosis. Which of the following statements regarding this scenario is correct?",
      "options": [
        "A. Coexisting tuberculous mediastinal lymphadenopathy and calcified nodes can obscure or create diagnostic interference during Sestamibi localization of an ectopic parathyroid adenoma",
        "B. Embryologically, ectopic parathyroid glands originate exclusively from the first pharyngeal pouch and migrate superiorly into the thyroid parenchyma",
        "C. The presence of mediastinal lymphadenopathy rules out primary hyperparathyroidism and confirms isolated extra-renal 1α-hydroxylase production",
        "D. 99mTc-Sestamibi scan uptake is entirely specific for tuberculous granulomas and cannot be retained by parathyroid tissue"
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "A",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "Parathyroid glands 在胚胎發育過程中（Embryology）隨 Branchial pouches 下降。若發育停滯或異常遷移，Ectopic parathyroid tissue 可能位於 Mediastinum 或 Chest。當患者發生 Primary hyperparathyroidism 且伴隨 Ectopic parathyroid adenoma 時，會持續分泌 PTH，引起 Hypercalcemia、Hypophosphatemia 與 Hyperparathyroidism。然而，若患者同時合併 Tuberculous mediastinal lymphadenopathy 或 Calcified nodes，這些縱隔腔病變在 Computed tomography (CT) 或 99mTc-Sestamibi scan / SPECT/CT 上可能會引發偽陽性吸收、解剖結構掩蓋或訊號干擾，干擾 Ectopic parathyroid adenoma 的精確定位（Localization interference）。\n\n- Option B 錯誤：Superior parathyroid glands 來自 Third pharyngeal pouch / Fourth pharyngeal pouch，Inferior parathyroid glands 來自 Third pharyngeal pouch，胚胎遷移方向為向下進入 Mediastinum，而非自 First pharyngeal pouch 向上遷移。\n- Option C 錯誤：Elevated PTH (210 pg/mL) 配合 Hypercalcemia 與 Hypophosphatemia 確診為 Primary hyperparathyroidism，非單純 Granulomatous extra-renal 1α-hydroxylase production（後者 PTH 應受抑制）。\n- Option D 錯誤：99mTc-Sestamibi 會被富含 Mitochondria 的 Parathyroid adenoma 顯著攝取並滯留（Retention），並非 Tuberculosis 專一性。",
