      "questionNumber": 12,
      "stem": "A 55-year-old woman with diabetic kidney disease undergoes renal biopsy for rapid decline in kidney function. Direct immunofluorescence shows smooth linear IgG staining along the glomerular basement membrane (GBM). The pathologist needs to distinguish whether this represents non-specific linear staining of diabetic nephropathy versus true Anti-GBM glomerulonephritis. Which set of findings most strongly supports a diagnosis of true Anti-GBM disease over diabetic nephropathy?",
      "options": [
        "A. Presence of extensive necrotizing crescents on light microscopy, circulating anti-α3(IV)NC1 antibodies, and concomitant pulmonary hemorrhage",
        "B. Presence of Kimmelstiel-Wilson nodules, diffuse mesangial matrix expansion, and negative circulating anti-GBM antibodies",
        "C. Absence of cellular crescents, linear IF staining positive for Albumin, and severe arteriolar hyalinosis",
        "D. Diffuse effacement of podocyte foot processes on electron microscopy with diffuse subepithelial spikes on silver stain"
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "NONE",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "要將 True Anti-GBM disease（Goodpasture syndrome）與 Diabetic nephropathy 的 Pseudo-linear IF staining 進行臨床與病理鑑別，極為關鍵。True Anti-GBM disease 的核心診斷依據包括：Light microscopy 顯示 Extensive necrotizing crescentic glomerulonephritis（Cellular crescents）、血清中檢出 Circulating anti-α3(IV)NC1 antibodies、臨床上可能合併 Pulmonary hemorrhage（Goodpasture syndrome），且其 IF 的 Linear IgG staining 通常不伴隨同等強度的 Albumin 陷留。相對地，Diabetic nephropathy 雖然具有 Linear IF staining，但顯微鏡下為 Kimmelstiel-Wilson nodules 與 Arteriolar hyalinosis，缺少 Crescent formation、無 Pulmonary hemorrhage，且 Circulating anti-GBM antibodies 為 Negative。\n\n- Option B 錯誤：此組合完美符合 Diabetic nephropathy，非 True Anti-GBM disease。\n- Option C 錯誤：缺乏 Cellular crescents 與雙重標定 Albumin 正確指向 Diabetic nephropathy 的非特異性吸附。\n- Option D 錯誤：此為 Membranous nephropathy 的光顯與電顯特徵。",
