      "questionNumber": 13,
      "stem": "A 68-year-old male with long-standing type 2 diabetes mellitus presents with acute kidney injury (serum creatinine 4.5 mg/dL), gross hematuria, and heavy proteinuria while hospitalized for an active methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) skin abscess. Renal biopsy reveals endocapillary proliferative glomerulonephritis with prominent neutrophil infiltration. Immunofluorescence (IF) demonstrates intense IgA and C3 immune deposits in a mesangial and capillary loop pattern. Electron microscopy (EM) shows scattered subepithelial electron-dense humps. Which of the following clinical and pathological findings most strongly supports Staphylococcus-associated post-infectious glomerulonephritis (PIGN) over primary IgA Nephropathy?",
      "options": [
        "A. Absence of C3 co-deposition on immunofluorescence microscopy",
        "B. Presence of active bacterial infection, endocapillary hypercellularity, and subepithelial electron-dense humps",
        "C. Universal requirement of persistent hypocomplementemia with low serum C3 in adult patients",
        "D. Asymptomatic microhematuria with normal renal function and absence of subepithelial deposits"
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "NONE",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "Staphylococcus-associated PIGN 常發生於年長者、Diabetic 族群或處於 active MRSA (如 Skin abscess、Osteomyelitis、Endocarditis) 感染狀態的患者。其 Immunofluorescence (IF) 常呈現 IgA-dominant 或 IgA co-dominant 的 Mesangial 及 Capillary loop 沉積，易與 IgA nephropathy 混淆。分辨二者的關鍵特徵包含：Concurrent active bacterial infection、Light microscopy 上的 Endocapillary proliferation (伴隨 Neutrophil 浸潤) 以及 Electron microscopy (EM) 上的 Subepithelial humps。值得注意的是，成年人的 Staphylococcus-associated PIGN 患者中，Serum C3 可為正常或僅短暫下降，故正常 Serum C3 不能排除 PIGN。",
