      "questionNumber": 14,
      "stem": "A 74-year-old female with diabetes mellitus develops severe acute kidney injury, proteinuria, and dysmorphic red blood cell casts following Staphylococcus aureus septic arthritis. A kidney biopsy is performed. Which of the following statements regarding the immunopathological features of Staphylococcus-associated post-infectious glomerulonephritis (PIGN) is CORRECT?",
      "options": [
        "A. Glomerular basement membranes show mandatory linear IgG deposition along capillary walls.",
        "B. Electron microscopy typically reveals subendothelial dense deposits without subepithelial hump formation.",
        "C. Immunofluorescence frequently reveals IgA-dominant or IgA co-dominant mesangial and capillary loop immune deposits, mimicking primary IgA Nephropathy.",
        "D. Serum C3 levels are severely suppressed in 100% of adult patients throughout the disease course."
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "NONE",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "Staphylococcus-associated PIGN 在 Immunofluorescence (IF) 鏡檢下的典型表現為 IgA-dominant 或 IgA co-dominant 的 Mesangial 及 Glomerular capillary loop 免疫複合物沉積，此現象極易被誤診為 Primary IgA nephropathy。然而，Staphylococcus-associated PIGN 在 Light microscopy (LM) 上常展現顯著的 Endocapillary hypercellularity 與 Neutrophil 浸潤，且 Electron microscopy (EM) 會觀察到大型 Subepithelial humps。此外，與兒童 Post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis (PSGN) 不同，成人 Staphylococcus-associated PIGN 患者的 Serum C3 不一定持續低下，部分患者 Serum C3 可維持在 Normal range。",
