      "stem": "A 22-year-old male presents with macrohematuria (cola-colored urine) that began 24 hours after the onset of fever, sore throat, and nasal congestion. Laboratory testing reveals a normal serum creatinine of 0.8 mg/dL and normal serum C3 and C4 complement levels. Which of the following diagnosis and clinical timing characteristics is most compatible with this presentation?",
      "options": [
        "A. IgA Nephropathy; characterized by synpharyngitic gross hematuria occurring concurrently or within 1-2 days of an upper respiratory infection with normal serum C3.",
        "B. Post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis; characterized by synpharyngitic onset within 24 hours and persistent hypocomplementemia.",
        "C. IgA Nephropathy; characterized by a typical post-infectious latent period of 2 to 6 weeks following dermal infection.",
        "D. Post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis; characterized by a 1 to 3 week post-pharyngeal latent period accompanied by normal complement levels."
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "NONE",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "IgA nephropathy 與 Post-infectious GN (PIGN / PSGN) 的臨床鑑別診斷中，Symptom onset timing 與 Serum complement 水平為關鍵指標：\n1. IgA nephropathy 典型表現為 Synpharyngitic hematuria，即在 Upper respiratory tract infection (URI) 發作的 Concurrent 時段或僅 1-2 天內即出現 Gross hematuria，且 Serum C3 水平通常保持 Normal。\n2. Post-infectious GN (如 PSGN) 則具有明顯的 Latent period，Pharyngeal infection 後需經過 1-3 週 (或 Dermal infection 後經過 2-6 週) 才會出現 Nephritic syndrome，且急性期幾乎皆伴隨 Low serum C3 (補體耗竭)，Serum C3 多在 6-8 週內恢復 Normal。",
