      "questionNumber": 19,
      "stem": "A 65-year-old male with Heart Failure with Reduced Ejection Fraction (HFrEF) and baseline chronic kidney disease stage 3a (serum creatinine 1.5 mg/dL, eGFR 48 mL/min/1.73 m²) is initiated on Sacubitril/Valsartan (Angiotensin Receptor-Neprilysin Inhibitor, ARNI). Two weeks later, repeat blood tests show serum creatinine 1.7 mg/dL (eGFR 41 mL/min/1.73 m²), serum potassium 4.7 mEq/L, and blood pressure 118/74 mmHg. Which of the following best describes the intrarenal hemodynamic mechanisms of Sacubitril/Valsartan and the appropriate clinical management?",
      "options": [
        "A. Sacubitril inhibits Neprilysin to increase natriuretic peptides, inducing afferent arteriolar vasodilation, while Valsartan blocks Angiotensin II type 1 receptors, inducing efferent arteriolar vasodilation; the transient eGFR drop is an acceptable hemodynamic effect, and therapy should be continued.",
        "B. Sacubitril causes selective efferent arteriolar vasoconstriction while Valsartan causes afferent arteriolar vasodilation; the increase in serum creatinine indicates drug-induced nephrotoxicity requiring immediate drug cessation.",
        "C. Both Sacubitril and Valsartan induce potent renal afferent arteriolar vasoconstriction to reduce intraglomerular hydrostatic pressure; Sacubitril/Valsartan should be promptly switched to an ACE inhibitor.",
        "D. Neprilysin inhibition by Sacubitril directly decreases glomerular capillary permeability surface area, whereas Valsartan increases efferent arteriolar tone; the transient eGFR decline requires dose reduction by 50%."
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "NONE",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "本題考驗 ARNI (Sacubitril/Valsartan) 的雙重機轉與 Renal Hemodynamics。\n1. Sacubitril 抑制 Neprilysin (NEP)，減少 ANP 與 BNP 的降解。ANP 與 BNP 作用於 Renal Afferent Arteriole，促進 Afferent Arteriolar Vasodilation，同時促進 Natriuresis 與 Diuresis。\n2. Valsartan 為 ARB，選擇性阻斷 Angiotensin II Type 1 Receptor (AT1 Receptor)，解除 Angiotensin II 所致的 Efferent Arteriolar Vasoconstriction，引發 Efferent Arteriolar Vasodilation，進而降低 Intraglomerular Hydrostatic Pressure (Pgc)。\n3. 在 Initiate ARNI 治療初期，由於 Efferent Arteriolar Vasodilation 導致 Intraglomerular Pressure 下降，可能出現 Transient Small Drop in eGFR (或 Serum Creatinine 輕微上升)。若 Serum Creatinine 上升幅度未超過 baseline 的 30%，且未伴隨 Severe Hyperkalemia 或 Persistent Hypotension，此為預期的 Hemodynamic Effect，代表 Glomerular Capillary Pressure 獲得舒緩，應繼續 Monitor 並維持原劑量治療。\n綜合以上，Option A 描述完全正確。",
      "resolvedImages": [
