      "questionNumber": 20,
      "stem": "Which of the following statements regarding the intrarenal hemodynamic effects and clinical monitoring of Sacubitril/Valsartan (ARNI) therapy is correct?",
      "options": [
        "A. Neprilysin inhibition leads to increased breakdown of Angiotensin II, which directly dilates the afferent arteriole and increases filtration fraction.",
        "B. Combined Neprilysin inhibition and Angiotensin receptor blockade reduce intraglomerular capillary hydraulic pressure by simultaneously dilating afferent arterioles (via natriuretic peptides) and efferent arterioles (via AT1 receptor blockade).",
        "C. An increase in serum creatinine of greater than 5% within 4 weeks of starting Sacubitril/Valsartan represents irreversible acute tubular necrosis and mandates immediate drug withdrawal.",
        "D. Sacubitril/Valsartan impairs renal autoregulation by selectively constricting both afferent and efferent arterioles, resulting in a dramatic increase in intraglomerular pressure and heavy proteinuria."
      ],
      "sourceProvidedAnswer": "NONE",
      "sourceAnswerStatus": "synthetic_tonks",
      "sourceExplanation": "本題考驗 Sacubitril/Valsartan 對於 Intrarenal Hemodynamics 的作用機制與 Clinical Monitoring 標準。\n1. Neprilysin (NEP) 抑制劑 Sacubitril 增加體內 ANP 與 BNP 濃度，造成 Afferent Arteriolar Vasodilation；Valsartan 則阻斷 AT1 Receptor，造成 Efferent Arteriolar Vasodilation。雙重作用共同降低 Intraglomerular Capillary Hydraulic Pressure (Pgc)，進而保護 Glomerulus。故 Option B 描述完全正確。\n2. 錯選項解析：\n   - Option A 錯誤：Neprilysin 亦參與 Angiotensin II 的降解，故 Neprilysin Inhibition 理論上會使 Angiotensin II 累積，這正是 Sacubitril 必須與 ARB (Valsartan) 聯合使用以阻斷 AT1 Receptor 的原因，而非直接舒張 Afferent Arteriole。\n   - Option C 錯誤：Serum Creatinine 上升小於 30% 為可接受之 Hemodynamic Change，絕非 Acute Tubular Necrosis，不需立即 Stoppage。\n   - Option D 錯誤：Sacubitril/Valsartan 舒張 Efferent Arteriole 並降低 Intraglomerular Pressure，可減少 Proteinuria，而非造成 Heavy Proteinuria。",
